Ideas for Controllers (src and test), checked against the code of FearlessLang/Controllers#61 and not applied there.

= Decisions for the user: the code and ControllersDesign disagree =

- An idle project with a problem (a file name Fearless rejects, a missing folder) is badged "data: invalid content"; ManagerTest asserts it. The design lists idle as its own state and gives invalid states only to code and data.
- Names.free adds a leading "p" to any invalid base: a folder named con becomes pcon (NamesTest asserts it). The design gives the "p" only to a name starting with a digit, then takes the first free valid name, which gives con2. The 64 character cut of long folder names is not in the design.
- Edit project metadata can change a kind outside idle (code to data directly) and can change the kind or path of a busy project; the kind request refuses both. Either commit refuses them, or the design exempts the editor.
- A kind request to the same kind (code to code) is silently accepted; the design refuses a change that is not from idle or back to idle.
- Content assist proposes the methods right after a closing bracket (foo()| and (x)|), inserted with no space; the design says after a dot, or after a space following an expression.
- The Panel's "Open docs" button duplicates Project > View documentation and is not in the design's panel list; the status bar is not in it either.
- Delete log removes the file on the Swing thread, outside the request queue; the design says everything the manager does for a project is a request.
- The design text should say: a tagged text on a one line spot (activity.txt, a register message) is never Str: when it holds a newline; a metadata commit whose base is no longer what projects.info holds is refused; names are the first valid one of name, name2...; methods of a type the last compile does not know come without documentation; Info values nest at most 100 deep.

= Manager GUI, from the full manual suite (allTests.txt) =

- The split divider does not resize the panes while dragged (the JSplitPane is not continuous layout); a drag toward the right edge once stopped at about a quarter of the screen.
- A second launch showing the window again moves the divider (about 390 to 1140 pixels).
- The mains list shows about three rows even with a large empty window, and its scroll arrow moves a few pixels per click.
- allTests.txt is stale: an added non empty project starts idle (Become code before Compile); Compile, Run, Run selected and Terminate are one button; a single main has no check box; TEST 1 needs a file manager refresh (F5) before the icon changes; TEST 9 "Compile enabled again, Run selected enabled" can not hold with one button; TEST 5 step 3 proves little with one project.

= Bugs and robustness not yet fixed =

- Windows, to check there: Deployed.compile passes the project folder as a command line argument; a name outside the ANSI code page, or a Base16: folder with an unpaired surrogate, likely reaches ChildMain mangled. A TaggedText.line argument is ASCII. Coordinator.runData has the same shape for runs.
- Windows, to check there: a Base16: path with an unpaired surrogate can reach tell or output inside a message, and writing console.txt then fails to encode it.
- File errors writing the eclipse folder (Eclipse.append, replace, publish, the console resets in Manager.load, open and clear) crash unclassified; a couldNotWriteEclipseFolder message would classify them as projects.info failures are.
- Eclipse.report lists the logs, then JUnitReport.suite lists them again: a log vanishing in between replaces the last good report.xml with an empty one. In Coordinator, JUnitReport.write and JUnitReport.file have no callers; one JUnitReport.report(folder,name,since) would serve Eclipse.report and remove them.
- Manager.commitNow reads the old console.txt with Fs.readUtf8; a console.txt deleted by hand, then a rename through metadata, crashes the manager.
- Manager.apply: a lone path message with a trailing newline ("path\n") is read as a request whose verb is the path.
- Manager.rotate can land on the selected project, so with two projects the other is checked every 6 seconds instead of 3.
- Manager.scan re-reads the mains whenever Facts changes, including a new log or an edited readme; only pkgs, hasCache, upToDate and problem matter.
- suggest.Api.Json.str never checks that it starts at a quote, so a malformed _map.json value like out" is read as ut.
- The plugin names its messages currentTimeMillis plus a UUID: two in the same millisecond are applied in UUID order, not in arrival order.
- Registry.real catches every IOException; only NoSuchFileException is a missing folder.
- Panel.fillMains shows an empty box for a compiled code project with no main.
- Tiles: arrow keys move the highlight without sending select; the next render snaps it back.
- Tiles.images caches icons keyed on the whole Project, so any job or time change misses the cache.
- Info.join prints an object inside a list at indent 0 (not reached today: lists hold only strings).
- Tokens.Kind.hidden() relies on ordinal() < 3: reordering the enum silently changes which tokens are hidden.
- Messages.unknownKind names the folder, while every other request refusal names the project; the clean request refuses as "clear cache refused", while every other refusal is named after its verb.
- The Facts icon cache (decoded images by file and stamp) is never pruned.
- Paths are written with '/' in projects.info but with the native separator in state.info, manager.info and activity.txt (a Windows only difference; the design shows both forms).

