- ManagerTest still uses assertTrue(...endsWith(...)) where the guide asks for utils.Err.

= Smaller code =

- Info.print through Join.of (one recursive show) instead of write, join and writeObj: about -24 lines.
- Info factories (obj, field, str, lst) shared by Eclipse and Registry instead of spelled out new Field(k,Info.noSpan,new Info.Str(x,Info.noSpan)).
- Fs.list(Path, Walk<T>) in Commons, next to Fs.walk, for the Files.list lambdas left (needs a new Commons.jar).
- Registry.writeText and Eclipse.replace are two versions of write a tmp file then atomic move; Main.leave is a third.
- Manager.publish renders the old state.info text again on every change, and load publishes it itself; a String published field removes both.
- Registry.problemIn repeats named(alias).
- The kinds list is written in Registry.kinds and Messages.unknownKind ("or" and "and"); the project name rules in Registry.fromInfo and Messages.projectNamed; derive or share them.
- A Manager line(f,text) helper for the "--- ... ---\n" Output frames.
- Lenient kind parsing with a sink for reset aliases could replace Registry.badKinds and both idle methods (about -6 lines).
- Registry's reader methods pass source through seven methods only to build errors; a private record holding it removes about 25 arguments.
- Project.running() returns Optional<String> only to be turned into "" by its one caller.
- new State(List.of(),Optional.empty()) appears in Manager, Window and Tiles.
- ChildMain and Main.main repeat the same exit code ladder (1, 2, 3).
- Main.run: catch(OverlappingFileLockException){ throw Bug.unreachable(); } adds nothing to the crash path.

= Separation of concerns =

- The design asks for a Report/Violation classification inside Controllers: Messages is split only by comments, Registry.Refused lives in Registry, and refusal texts are written inline in Manager, Registry, Names.markerProblem, Facts.of, Window and Panel.
- The projects.info schema (fromInfo, entryOf, pathOf, kindOf, names, aliasMap, toInfo, entryToInfo) as its own class, apart from the in memory registry and persistence.
- Manager.Live mixes project long fields and per job fields; a Job object, null when idle, would simplify busy, exited, terminate, drop and refused.
- A Verb enum (takes a third line, selects) instead of the parallel lists verbs, thirdLine and the inline select list.
- Compile and run times live in Registry.Entry although the design says they are not metadata, so every compile start and main start rewrites projects.info.
- Facts.of sets the global UserError.root as a side effect, and Deployed.mains relies on it; set it where the compiler is called.
- Manager.State and Project.State are unrelated types with the same name, both used in Tiles.

= Style =

- for( / while( / switch( and for ( / while ( / switch ( are mixed; suggest writes f(a, b) where controller and gui write f(a,b); Sni and Pilot use i++ and C style loops.
- Long inline lambdas: Registry.badKinds, Manager.commitNow's renamed map, Eclipse.report, Resolver.params, Resolver.declaration, Tray.install's gone listener.
- Pilot.pause throws new RuntimeException(e) where Pilot.robot uses Bug.of(e); ChildMain is not final; Collapsible calls toLowerCase() without Locale.ROOT; Panel.shown is typed Object; two methods named Eclipse.report do different things.

= Refused =

- Checking the launcher name in Association.identity (design: File associations): FearlessLang/Controllers#55 deliberately does not check it. Related and still open: the console launcher and its windowed "w" twin are two association identities, so starting them alternately rewrites the associations each time.
